      "title": "Undo Mental Model: Three Areas",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Undo Mental Model: Three Areas",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Three Areas",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Working tree",
                    "sub": "files on disk",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Index",
                    "sub": "staging, `git add`",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Repository",
                    "sub": "HEAD commit, `git commit`",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Every undo command targets ==one or more== of these areas",
                "Pick the area first, then pick the command"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Rewrite or Append",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "History",
                "Undo by"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "{green:Local, unpublished}",
                  "==Rewrite== it: reset, amend"
                ],
                [
                  "{red:Pushed, shared}",
                  "==Add new commits== only: revert"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Check Before Undoing",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`git status` shows which area holds the change",
                "`git log --oneline -5` shows the latest commits",
                "Run both ==before== any undo"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. What Can Be Lost",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "State",
                "Recovery"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Committed",
                  "{green:Reflog} ~**90 days**; unreachable ~**30 days**, until gc"
                ],
                [
                  "Never committed",
                  "{red:None}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "No way back",
              "text": "`git restore` and `reset --hard` on ==never-committed== edits cannot be undone."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Restore and Unstage Files",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Restore and Unstage Files",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What restore targets",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Command",
                "Effect"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`git restore <file>`",
                  "worktree ← index; {red:edits gone}"
                ],
                [
                  "`git restore --staged <file>`",
                  "unstage; {green:edits kept}"
                ],
                [
                  "`git restore --source=<c> <file>`",
                  "file from any commit → worktree"
                ],
                [
                  "`--staged --worktree`",
                  "updates index and worktree"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "No undo",
              "text": "Discarded uncommitted edits are ==unrecoverable==: never committed, so not in the reflog."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Source and hunks",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`--source` takes any commit: `HEAD~2`, a branch, a tag",
                "`-p` asks per hunk: ==y== discard, ==n== keep, ==s== split",
                "Other hunks in the file stay untouched"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "git restore --source=HEAD~2 app.py",
                "git restore --source=HEAD~2 --staged --worktree app.py",
                "git restore -p app.py"
              ],
              "note": "old content into worktree; into both; chosen hunks only"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Older equivalents",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Older",
                "Modern"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`git checkout -- <file>`",
                  "`git restore <file>`"
                ],
                [
                  "`git reset HEAD <file>`",
                  "`git restore --staged <file>`"
                ],
                [
                  "`git checkout <c> -- <file>`",
                  "`git restore --source=<c> <file>`"
                ]
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Reset: Soft, Mixed, Hard",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Reset: Soft, Mixed, Hard",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What reset moves",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`git reset <commit>` moves the ==current branch pointer== to that commit",
                "The **mode** decides what else is rewound: index, working tree"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Mode",
                "Moves",
                "Your changes"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`--soft`",
                  "HEAD",
                  "{green:staged}"
                ],
                [
                  "`--mixed` (default)",
                  "HEAD + index",
                  "{orange:unstaged}, still on disk"
                ],
                [
                  "`--hard`",
                  "HEAD + index + worktree",
                  "{red:lost}"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Undo recent commits",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`--soft HEAD~1` undoes the last commit, files stay staged",
                "Ideal for ==redoing or squashing== the last commits",
                "`HEAD~3` goes back three commits"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "git reset --soft HEAD~1   # keep staged",
                "git reset HEAD~3          # mixed: unstaged"
              ],
              "note": "soft keeps the index; mixed drops it"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Hard reset and the way out",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`--hard` discards uncommitted edits, so run ==git status== first",
                "`ORIG_HEAD` records the previous tip, so it undoes a bad merge or reset"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "git reset --hard ORIG_HEAD"
              ],
              "note": "back to the tip before the merge or reset"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Never-committed edits",
              "text": "`reset --hard` on edits that were **never committed** cannot be undone."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Amend and Revert",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Amend and Revert",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Amend the last commit",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`git commit --amend` ==replaces== the last commit",
                "Fix its message, or stage more files and add them without a new commit",
                "`--no-edit` keeps the message and adds the newly staged changes"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "git add forgotten.txt",
                "git commit --amend --no-edit"
              ],
              "note": "adds the file, same message"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Amend rewrites history",
              "text": "Amend creates a ==new commit hash==. Never amend a commit that is already pushed."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Revert a commit",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`git revert <commit>` adds a ==new commit== that inverts those changes",
                "History stays intact, so it is safe on shared branches",
                "`-m 1` selects the ==mainline parent== (1 = the branch you merged into)",
                "`A..B` reverts a range of commits",
                "`-n` stages the reverts without committing, so they fold into ==one commit=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "git revert <commit>",
                "git revert -m 1 <merge-commit>",
                "git revert -n A..B",
                "git commit -m \"revert A..B\""
              ],
              "note": "single, merge, then a range as one commit"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "amend",
                "revert"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "History",
                  "replaces tip, new hash",
                  "adds a commit"
                ],
                [
                  "Use when",
                  "local, unpushed",
                  "pushed, shared"
                ]
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Reflog and Recovering Lost Work",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Reflog and Recovering Lost Work",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What the Reflog Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`git reflog` lists where ==HEAD== (and each branch) pointed over time",
                "Entries look like `HEAD@{2}`: two moves ago",
                "==Local only==: never pushed to a remote"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Recovery Recipes",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Lost",
                "Find it",
                "Restore"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Bad reset / rebase",
                  "`git reflog`, pre-mistake entry",
                  "`git reset --hard HEAD@{n}`"
                ],
                [
                  "Deleted branch",
                  "`git reflog`, last commit hash",
                  "`git branch <name> <hash>`"
                ],
                [
                  "Dropped stash / dangling commit",
                  "`git fsck --lost-found`",
                  "`git branch <name> <hash>`"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`git branch -D` deletes the ==label only==",
                "Commits remain until gc, so recovery is **quick**"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "git branch -D feature",
                "git reflog                   # find its last hash",
                "git branch feature a1b2c3d   # label is back"
              ],
              "note": "recreate a deleted branch"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Time Limit",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Reachable entries expire after ==90 days==",
                "Unreachable entries expire after ==30 days=="
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Recover promptly",
              "text": "Once an entry expires, gc can prune the commit for good. Run `git reflog` **first**, before anything else."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Undoing Pushed Commits Safely: Cheat Sheet",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Undoing Pushed Commits Safely: Cheat Sheet",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Decision Rule",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Situation",
                "Do"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Local, unpushed",
                  "{green:reset} or {green:amend}"
                ],
                [
                  "Pushed, shared",
                  "{blue:revert}"
                ],
                [
                  "Panicking",
                  "{red:reflog first}"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Pushed Commits",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Shared branch: ==git revert <hash>==, then a normal `git push`",
                "No force needed: history only grows",
                "Rewriting your own pushed branch: ==--force-with-lease==, it refuses if the remote has new commits"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Never `reset` or `amend` on main or any branch teammates pulled",
                "Never bare `--force`: it overwrites blind"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "git revert <hash>",
                "git push",
                "git push --force-with-lease"
              ],
              "note": "revert for shared, lease only for your own branch"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Cheat Sheet",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Goal",
                "Command"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "File edit",
                  "`restore <f>`"
                ],
                [
                  "Unstage",
                  "`restore --staged <f>`"
                ],
                [
                  "Last commit",
                  "`reset --soft HEAD~1`"
                ],
                [
                  "Discard all",
                  "`reset --hard`"
                ],
                [
                  "Shared commit",
                  "`revert`"
                ],
                [
                  "Lost commit",
                  "`reflog` + `reset --hard HEAD@{n}`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Did anyone else pull it? ==Yes: revert.== No: reset or amend."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "You run `git reset --soft HEAD~1`. Where do the undone commit's changes end up?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Staged in the index",
                "`--soft` moves only HEAD",
                "`--mixed` would leave them unstaged"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "You edited a file and never staged or committed it, then ran `git restore file`. Can the edits be recovered?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "No, Git never saw them",
                "reflog tracks only ref moves"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "A bad commit is already pushed to main. Which command is right: reset --hard or revert?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "`git revert <hash>`, then a normal push",
                "It adds a new commit and rewrites nothing",
                "`reset --hard` would break teammates' history"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "You deleted a branch with `git branch -D feat`. How do you get it back?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "`git reflog`, find the branch's last commit hash",
                "`git branch feat <hash>`",
                "Only the label was deleted, commits remain until gc"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}